window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["27"]={"https://theconversation.com/gibran-mundur-koalisi-membuktikan-bahwa-kesetiaan-politik-hanya-soal-kepentingan-296497":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"0fa10a3f913584de7c81659c4d2db3f6e143eb7670383848bbea24365ca75ac7","read":"https://theconversation.com/gibran-mundur-koalisi-membuktikan-bahwa-kesetiaan-politik-hanya-soal-kepentingan-296497","bytes":181246,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Gibran mundur, koalisi membuktikan bahwa kesetiaan politik hanya soal kepentingan","by":[{"n":"Wildan Rofii","r":"Research Assistant dan Master Student di Political Sciences, Universitas Islam Internasional Indonesia (UIII)"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T08:05:13Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["• Koalisi Prabowo-Gibran tetap utuh, tetapi dukungan terhadap Gibran menghilang."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Dulu Gibran menjadi penengah koalisi sekaligus simbol politik Jokowi."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Gibran mundur, Jokowi kehilangan ‘menteri’ terkuat di papan kekuasaan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Gibran Rakabuming Raka ",["telah menyerahkan surat pengunduran dirinya dari jabatan Wakil Presiden (wapres) ke Majelis Permusyawaratan Rakyat (MPR)","https://www.bbc.com/indonesia/articles/cw7v25ry790zo"]," pada Kamis, 12 November siang hari. Keputusan ini mengakhiri perjalanan politiknya di pemerintahan yang genap dua tahun pada akhir Oktober silam."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mundurnya Gibran dari kursi wapres menimbulkan pertanyaan besar: mengapa koalisi yang dulu begitu kuat mendukung Gibran kini nyaris tidak membelanya?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Kemenangan Prabowo: efek Jokowi dan ujian demokrasi Indonesia","https://theconversation.com/kemenangan-prabowo-efek-jokowi-dan-ujian-demokrasi-indonesia-223603"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Sebanyak 120 anggota DPR dari delapan fraksi mendukung ",["usulan Hak Menyatakan Pendapat (HMP)","https://nasional.kompas.com/read/2026/11/10/14303301/hak-menyatakan-pendapat-ijazah-gibran-hampir-50-anggota-dpr-tanda-tangan"]," terkait polemik dokumen pendidikan Gibran. Di tengah tekanan tersebut, dukungan terbuka dari partai-partai koalisi terhadapnya hampir tidak terdengar. Salah satu yang ",["menyatakan siap mengawal Gibran","https://kabar24.bisnis.com/read/20261015/15/2012894/psi-siap-kawal-gibran-di-tengah-desakan-pemakzulan"]," adalah Partai Solidaritas Indonesia (PSI), tetapi partai ini tidak memiliki kursi di DPR."]},{"k":"p","s":["Situasi ini memperlihatkan ironi politik Indonesia. Koalisi pendukung Prabowo-Gibran masih bertahan, tetapi salah satu tokoh yang mengantarkan mereka ke kekuasaan justru kehilangan dukungan politik."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mengapa koalisi yang sama tidak lagi melindungi Gibran? Dan apa arti pengunduran diri ini bagi masa depan politik Jokowi?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Fungsi Gibran sudah tidak lagi dibutuhkan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Untuk memahami perubahan sikap koalisi, kita perlu melihat kembali alasan Gibran dipilih sebagai calon wakil presiden Prabowo pada 2023."]},{"k":"p","s":["Setidaknya, ada dua fungsi politik yang membuat Gibran penting bagi Koalisi Indonesia Maju (KIM)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pertama, Gibran menjadi jalan tengah bagi kepentingan partai-partai koalisi. Saat itu, sejumlah partai memiliki ",["kandidat masing-masing untuk posisi cawapres","https://www.kompas.tv/nasional/450505/pan-sambut-baik-usulan-gibran-jadi-bakal-cawapres-prabowo-di-pilpres-2024"],". Golkar mendorong Airlangga Hartarto, PAN mengusulkan Erick Thohir, sedangkan Demokrat menginginkan Agus Harimurti Yudhoyono."]},{"k":"p","s":["Gibran menjadi pilihan yang relatif dapat diterima semua pihak. Ia bukan kader partai anggota KIM dan merupakan putra Presiden Joko Widodo. Dengan demikian, pencalonannya tidak harus mengorbankan kepentingan salah satu partai."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Gibran dan politikus muda lain yang lahir dari dinasti politik: pedang bermata dua bagi demokrasi","https://theconversation.com/gibran-dan-politikus-muda-lain-yang-lahir-dari-dinasti-politik-pedang-bermata-dua-bagi-demokrasi-125720"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Kedua, Gibran menjadi penghubung Prabowo dengan basis pendukung Jokowi. ",["Survei Politika Research and Consulting","https://politik.tvrinews.com/berita/tblrryz-survei-prc-elektabilitas-anies-muhaimin-naik-prabowo-gibran-turun-pilpres-2024-akan-berlangsung-2-putaran"]," mencatat 61,7% masyarakat yang puas terhadap kinerja Jokowi memilih pasangan Prabowo-Gibran pada Desember 2023 juga menunjukkan 61,7% masyarakat yang puas terhadap kinerja Jokowi memilih pasangan Prabowo-Gibran. Temuan senada juga dibuktikan dari ",["exit poll Litbang Kompas","https://nasional.kompas.com/read/2024/02/15/08063551/exit-poll-litbang-kompas-626-persen-responden-yang-puas-dengan-kinerja"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam ilmu politik, fenomena ini dikenal sebagai coattail effect (efek ekor jas), yakni keuntungan elektoral yang diperoleh kandidat atau partai karena popularitas tokoh yang lebih kuat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, kedua fungsi tersebut kini tidak lagi bernilai sama."]},{"k":"p","s":["Setelah Prabowo menjadi presiden, perekat utama koalisi bukan lagi kebutuhan untuk mencari pasangan calon, melainkan akses terhadap kekuasaan pemerintahan. Koalisi juga berkembang menjadi KIM Plus dengan bergabungnya partai-partai lain, termasuk PKB dan NasDem."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dengan kata lain, posisi Prabowo sebagai presiden membuat Gibran tidak lagi menjadi figur yang dibutuhkan untuk menjaga keseimbangan koalisi."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ketika perisai politik menghilang"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pengunduran diri Gibran juga memperlihatkan persoalan lain: lemahnya dukungan politik ketika seorang pejabat menghadapi krisis legitimasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ilmuwan politik Aníbal Pérez-Liñán menjelaskan pentingnya ",["dukungan legislatif dalam mempertahankan kekuasaan seorang presiden","https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/presidential-impeachment-and-the-new-political-instability-in-latin-america/00B01667C5803F3AF795E5B72939FFC2"],". Ia menggunakan konsep legislative shield (perisai legislatif) untuk menggambarkan perlindungan politik yang diberikan anggota parlemen kepada pemimpin pemerintahan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Menurut Pérez-Liñán, skandal tidak selalu berujung pada jatuhnya seorang pemimpin. Risiko menjadi lebih besar ketika dukungan politik di parlemen ikut hilang."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Harta, jabatan, dan kekuasaan: bagaimana sistem presidensial dorong perpecahan partai politik di Indonesia","https://theconversation.com/harta-jabatan-dan-kekuasaan-bagaimana-sistem-presidensial-dorong-perpecahan-partai-politik-di-indonesia-158976"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Kerangka ini membantu menjelaskan situasi Gibran. Pada 2023, partai-partai koalisi memiliki kepentingan untuk mempertahankan pencalonannya meskipun muncul kontroversi etik terkait proses pencalonan. Kini, ketika persoalan dokumen pendidikannya berkembang menjadi persoalan hukum dan politik, dukungan tersebut tidak lagi terlihat."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Putusan Mahkamah Konstitusi dan Mahkamah Agung terkait dokumen pendidikan Gibran semakin memperbesar tekanan","https://www.cna.id/indonesia/pemakzulan-gibran-dpr-putusan-ma-mk-52841"],". Sebanyak 120 anggota DPR dari delapan fraksi kemudian mendukung usulan HMP yang dapat membuka jalan menuju proses pemakzulan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, penting dicatat bahwa persoalan hukum dan politik ini tidak boleh dicampuradukkan. Pengunduran diri merupakan keputusan politik, sedangkan keabsahan dokumen pendidikan harus dinilai berdasarkan putusan dan proses hukum yang berlaku."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yang patut dikritisi adalah sikap partai-partai politik. Ketika Gibran menguntungkan koalisi, mereka mendukung pencalonannya. Ketika ia menjadi beban politik, dukungan itu menghilang."]},{"k":"h","s":["Jokowi kehilangan ‘menteri’ politiknya"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pengunduran diri Gibran juga menjadi pukulan telak bagi posisi politik Jokowi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ibarat permainan catur, Jokowi adalah raja yang masih berada di papan, tetapi memiliki ruang gerak terbatas setelah tidak lagi menjabat presiden. Sementara itu, Gibran merupakan menteri yang memberinya akses langsung ke pusat kekuasaan pemerintahan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kehadiran Gibran sebagai wakil presiden memungkinkan Jokowi mempertahankan hubungan politik dengan pemerintahan baru. Kini, jalur tersebut tidak lagi tersedia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Memang, kehilangan jabatan wakil presiden tidak otomatis mengakhiri pengaruh politik Gibran maupun Jokowi. Namun, jabatan publik memberikan akses, visibilitas, jaringan, dan sumber daya politik yang tidak mudah digantikan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bagi Gibran, tantangannya adalah membangun kembali legitimasi politik tanpa jabatan strategis dan tanpa dukungan partai yang kuat di parlemen. Sementara bagi Jokowi, persoalannya adalah bagaimana mempertahankan pengaruh politik setelah kehilangan akses langsung ke pemerintahan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Apalagi, PSI yang selama ini menjadi kendaraan politik penting bagi Jokowi juga menghadapi persoalan internal. Mundurnya ",["sejumlah pengurus PSI","https://tirto.id/eks-elite-psi-di-kabinet-prabowo-ramai-ramai-mundur-ada-apa-idCj"]," semakin menambah ketidakpastian mengenai arah politik keluarga Jokowi menjelang Pemilu 2029."]},{"k":"h","s":["Koalisi setia pada kepentingan, bukan orang"]},{"k":"p","s":["Perubahan sikap terhadap Gibran sejalan dengan kajian mengenai ",["kartelisasi partai politik di Indonesia","https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/journal-of-east-asian-studies/article/party-cartelization-indonesianstyle-presidential-powersharing-and-the-contingency-of-democratic-opposition/1F94822ADC024F3D75F0666350FB9F14"]," yang menjelaskan bagaimana partai-partai politik cenderung membangun kerja sama untuk memperoleh dan mempertahankan akses terhadap kekuasaan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Buruknya demokrasi Indonesia setelah Orde Baru: dampak dari ‘negara bayangan’","https://theconversation.com/buruknya-demokrasi-indonesia-setelah-orde-baru-dampak-dari-negara-bayangan-250970"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam sistem seperti ini, persaingan politik tidak selalu berakhir dengan terbentuknya oposisi yang kuat. Partai-partai justru memiliki insentif untuk bergabung dengan pemerintahan demi mempertahankan pengaruh dan kepentingannya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kasus Gibran memperlihatkan konsekuensi dari pola tersebut. Dukungan politik tidak selalu dibangun atas dasar kesamaan ideologi, prinsip, atau tanggung jawab bersama. Dukungan dapat berubah ketika kepentingan para aktor politik berubah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Karena itu, pengunduran diri Gibran bukan sekadar persoalan masa depan seorang wakil presiden. Peristiwa ini juga membuka pertanyaan tentang kualitas koalisi politik di Indonesia: apakah partai-partai benar-benar memiliki komitmen politik yang konsisten, atau hanya berkumpul selama kekuasaan memberikan keuntungan?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Jika seorang tokoh yang dahulu menjadi bagian penting kemenangan koalisi gampang ditinggalkan ketika menghadapi masalah, publik patut mempertanyakan seberapa kuat sebenarnya ikatan politik di antara partai-partai tersebut."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada akhirnya, yang terlihat bukanlah koalisi yang setia kepada orang, tapi pada kekuasaan."]}],"chars":7804},"https://theconversation.com/saat-demokrasi-dilawan-dengan-represi-polisi-jadi-alat-pembungkam-kritik-294909":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"5583a0f319a60d8bb80da7518294fcf0a16eedfde9855533861ecb6ad37860cc","read":"https://theconversation.com/saat-demokrasi-dilawan-dengan-represi-polisi-jadi-alat-pembungkam-kritik-294909","bytes":180283,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Saat demokrasi dilawan dengan represi, polisi jadi alat pembungkam kritik","by":[{"n":"Aniello Iannone","r":"Lecturer, Universitas Diponegoro"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T06:22:40Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["• Polisi tidak hanya mengamankan demonstrasi, tetapi juga membatasi ruang demokrasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Kelompok marginal menghadapi kontrol dan kekerasan negara secara tidak setara."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Demokrasi membutuhkan perlindungan hak berekspresi, bukan sekadar ketertiban publik."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Penangkapan ratusan orang","https://lbhyogyakarta.org/perkembangan-pengaduan-dan-pendampingan"]," setelah demonstrasi di Yogyakarta pada 10 November 2026 menyisakan pertanyaan yang lebih besar daripada sekadar siapa yang terlibat dalam kericuhan."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Polda DIY menangkap 157 orang","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5847163/polda-diy-amankan-157-orang-terkait-kericuhan-termasuk-21-anak"]," setelah sekelompok massa terlibat pelemparan batu, petasan, dan bom molotov ke gedung DPRD. Namun, tim hukum BARA ADIL ",["menerima puluhan pengaduan","https://tirto.id/demo-jogja-10-november-64-aduan-lbh-dan-157-orang-ditangkap-idFQ"]," terkait penangkapan dan dugaan kekerasan aparat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Muncul pula ",["laporan mengenai pengejaran massa","https://jogja.idntimes.com/news/jogja/tudingan-represif-dan-rantis-masuk-ugm-ini-klarifikasi-kapolda-diy-00-6gk18-dwsbws"]," hingga kawasan sekitar kampus UGM. Namun ",["polisi membantah","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5847143/polda-diy-bantah-isu-personel-masuk-kampus-saat-pengamanan-unjuk-rasa"]," memasuki area kampus."]},{"k":"p","s":["Persoalan serupa terlihat dalam ",["demonstrasi mahasiswa di kawasan Tugu Tani","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5799121/ratusan-mahasiswa-unjuk-rasa-di-kawasan-tugu-tani"],", Jakarta, pada 20 Oktober 2026. Saat memperingati dua tahun pemerintahan Prabowo Subianto - Gibran Rakabuming, mahasiswa menyampaikan ",["lima tuntutan dan memasang spanduk","https://www.idntimes.com/news/indonesia/mahasiswa-naik-ke-atas-tugu-tani-pasang-baliho-berisi-tuntutan-00-jkxzp-22wgdn/amp"]," di monumen. Menjelang malam, ",["polisi menurunkan spanduk tersebut","https://www.suara.com/news/2026/10/20/193809/tembus-penjagaan-spanduk-protes-2-tahun-rezim-prabowo-berkibar-di-monumen-tugu-tani"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kita bisa lihat pola yang berulang. Demonstrasi berlangsung, polisi bertindak di lokasi, lalu massa membubarkan diri."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun di balik itu semua, kita perlu juga melihat dengan kritis bagaimana negara begitu sibuk mengatur bagaimana warga menyampaikan kritik, tetapi tidak selalu menunjukkan kesigapan yang sama dalam menjawabnya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketika ruang warga dibatasi, persoalannya bukan lagi sekadar ketertiban umum, melainkan hak warga untuk ikut menentukan arah kebijakan yang memengaruhi hidup mereka."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ruang demokrasi yang dikendalikan"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Filsuf dan pemikir politik Jerman, Hannah Arendt","https://press.uchicago.edu/ucp/books/book/chicago/H/bo3684031.html"],", menyebut bahwa ruang yang terbentuk ketika orang berkumpul untuk berbicara dan bertindak bersama sebagai space of appearance (ruang penampakan)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ruang ini tidak harus berupa gedung parlemen atau balai kota–bisa juga muncul ketika warga bertemu, menyampaikan pendapat, dan memperjuangkan kepentingan bersama. Contoh bentuknya adalah demonstrasi, rapat warga, mimbar bebas, dan aksi solidaritas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Menurut Arendt, kekuasaan lahir dari kemampuan manusia bertindak bersama, bukan semata-mata dari kekuatan aparat atau senjata. ",["Dalam “On Violence” (1970)","https://archive.org/details/onviolence0000aren"],", ia membedakan kekuasaan dari kekerasan: kekuasaan membutuhkan dukungan bersama, sedangkan kekerasan merupakan instrumen pemaksaan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pembedaan ini penting untuk memahami peran polisi. Polisi memang berkewajiban menjaga keselamatan demonstran dan masyarakat, termasuk mencegah perusakan serta kekerasan. Namun, tugas pengamanan tidak boleh berubah menjadi kewenangan untuk menentukan pendapat mana yang boleh disampaikan dan kapan kritik harus dihentikan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di Indonesia, ",["Peraturan Kapolri Nomor 7 Tahun 2012","https://www.pusdikmin.com/perpus/file/perkap-no-7-tahun-2012-ttg-pendapat-dimuka-umum.pdf"]," mengatur penyampaian pendapat di tempat terbuka pukul 06.00–18.00. Ketentuan ini berbeda dari ",["Undang-Undang Nomor 9 Tahun 1998","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/45478/uu-no-9-tahun-1998"]," yang menjamin kebebasan menyampaikan pendapat di muka umum."]},{"k":"p","s":["Persoalannya bukan semata-mata soal batas waktu, melainkan bagaimana aturan teknis diterapkan agar tidak mengurangi substansi hak konstitusional warga."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketika polisi lebih sibuk membatasi durasi demonstrasi daripada memastikan aspirasi warga diteruskan kepada pengambil keputusan, fungsi pengamanan berisiko bergeser menjadi pengendalian politik."]},{"k":"h","s":["Negara tak memperlakukan semua warga setara"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pembatasan ruang demokrasi tidak dialami semua kelompok secara setara. ",["Kajian kolonialisme oleh filsuf Frantz Fanon","https://groveatlantic.com/book/the-wretched-of-the-earth/"]," menggambarkan masyarakat kolonial sebagai dunia yang terbelah. Barak dan kantor polisi menjadi penanda batas kekuasaan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Polisi bukan sekadar penegak hukum, melainkan wajah langsung kekuasaan yang mengendalikan kehidupan penduduk jajahan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Indonesia tentu bukan masyarakat kolonial dalam pengertian yang dibahas Fanon. Namun, pemikirannya membantu kita melihat bagaimana aparat keamanan dapat menjadi titik kontak utama antara negara dan kelompok yang memiliki posisi tawar lebih lemah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bayangkan ",["warga miskin yang menghadapi penggusuran","https://bantuanhukum.or.id/warga-marunda-kepu-adukan-dugaan-penggusuran-paksa-ke-komnas-ham/"],", ",["petani yang mempertahankan tanah","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5462555/komnas-ham-soroti-risiko-kriminalisasi-warga-dalam-konflik-agrariam"],", atau ",["masyarakat adat yang menolak perampasan ruang hidup","https://www.hrw.org/news/2026/07/28/indonesia-environmentalists-indigenous-leaders-unjustly-prosecuted"],". Mereka tidak selalu memiliki akses yang sama kepada pejabat, pengacara, media, atau saluran pengaduan. Ketika protes menjadi satu-satunya cara agar persoalan mereka terlihat, ",["respons negara","https://www.hrw.org/report/2026/07/28/grabbed-land-silenced-justice/the-persecution-of-environmentalists-and-indigenous"]," yang mengutamakan pengerahan aparat justru memperlebar ketimpangan dan memperburuk persoalan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pola serupa terlihat di negara lain. ",["Di Delhi","https://www.reuters.com/world/india/delhi-sealed-off-ahead-youth-protest-against-indian-election-chief-2026-10-10"],", polisi India menahan lebih dari 2 ribu pendukung Partai Kecoak, gerakan anak muda yang menuntut pengunduran diri Ketua Komisi Pemilihan Umum India, Gyanesh Kumar."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Di Prancis","https://theprint.in/world/police-and-protesters-clash-in-some-of-frances-worst-unrest-in-years/3074936/"],", demonstrasi nasional menentang kenaikan biaya hidup pada 17 Oktober 2026 diwarnai bentrokan antara polisi dan demonstran. Seorang remaja berusia 17 tahun kehilangan tangannya setelah granat kejut yang digunakan aparat meledak di Saint-Étienne."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sementara itu, ",["di Rio de Janeiro","https://wapsphp.test.ohchr.un-icc.cloud/en/press-releases/2025/10/brazil-un-experts-urge-swift-investigation-deadly-police-operation-rio-de"],", operasi polisi di kawasan Penha dan Alemão pada tahun sebelumnya menewaskan 122 orang."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketiga peristiwa tersebut menunjukkan bahwa pengendalian negara atas ruang publik dapat mengambil bentuk berbeda, dari pembatasan partisipasi politik hingga kekerasan mematikan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam konteks Indonesia, ",["kematian pengemudi ojek daring Affan Kurniawan","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5072541/pengemudi-ojol-korban-insiden-rantis-brimob-dimakamkan"]," setelah terlindas kendaraan taktis Brimob pada Agustus 2025 memperlihatkan betapa seriusnya persoalan akuntabilitas aparat. Peristiwa tersebut menjadi pengingat bahwa penggunaan kekuatan negara memiliki konsekuensi langsung terhadap keselamatan warga."]},{"k":"h","s":["Menjaga ketertiban atau membungkam kritik?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tindakan polisi meredam massa ketika demonstrasi berubah menjadi kekerasan tentu beralasan. Pembakaran fasilitas publik, penyerangan, dan tindakan yang membahayakan orang lain tidak dapat dibenarkan atas nama kebebasan berekspresi. Negara berkewajiban melindungi keselamatan semua pihak."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, tindakan sebagian demonstran tidak boleh menjadi alasan untuk memperlakukan seluruh peserta aksi sebagai ancaman. Penggunaan kekuatan harus berdasarkan hukum, diperlukan, proporsional, dan dapat dipertanggungjawabkan. Kritik tidak identik dengan ancaman keamanan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Demokrasi tidak diukur dari seberapa tertib jalanan setelah demonstrasi dibubarkan. Demokrasi justru terlihat dari kesediaan pemerintah mendengar suara yang tidak menyenangkan, menjawab tuntutan yang dianggap mengganggu, dan membuka ruang bagi warga untuk mengoreksi kekuasaan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Polisi seharusnya menjaga agar ruang itu tetap aman, bukan menentukan siapa yang berhak menggunakannya. Sebab, ketika negara lebih cepat mengirim aparat daripada memberikan jawaban, yang menyempit bukan hanya ruang demonstrasi, melainkan juga ruang demokrasi itu sendiri."]}],"chars":6535},"https://theconversation.com/kasus-cornell-7-harus-jadi-alasan-kita-mengevaluasi-strategi-pencegahan-kekerasan-seksual-293809":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"621784121c9068ccaad4812a907739df47ff5a659f890b632125c3107576dadd","read":"https://theconversation.com/kasus-cornell-7-harus-jadi-alasan-kita-mengevaluasi-strategi-pencegahan-kekerasan-seksual-293809","bytes":187610,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Kasus Cornell 7 harus jadi alasan kita mengevaluasi strategi pencegahan kekerasan seksual","by":[{"n":"Sarah Vrankovich","r":"Research Fellow, La Trobe University"},{"n":"Camille Schloeffel","r":"PhD Candidate, Australian Research Centre in Sex, Health and Society, La Trobe University"},{"n":"Jessica Ison","r":"Senior Lecturer and Deputy Director, Reducing Gender-Based Violence Research Group, La Trobe University"}],"pub":"2026-10-07T06:09:04Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Kasus yang sedang berlangsung di Universitas Cornell, Amerika Serikat, memicu kemarahan publik yang meluas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seorang mantan mahasiswa, Jane Doe (nama samaran), mengajukan ",["gugatan perdata","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cmpq0r1ljpqwo"]," Ia melaporkan bahwa dirinya dibius dan diperkosa oleh tujuh anggota Chi Phi, suatu perkumpulan mahasiswa, pada Oktober 2024. Ia juga menuduh bahwa Universitas Cornell ",["gagal","https://www.mamamia.com.au/cornell-university-lawsuit/"]," memberikan perlindungan dan dukungan yang memadai."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Dugaan kasus kekerasan seksual FH UI: Bukti absennya etika gender dalam pendidikan hukum","https://theconversation.com/dugaan-kasus-kekerasan-seksual-fh-ui-bukti-absennya-etika-gender-dalam-pendidikan-hukum-280724"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Menurut ",["pemberitaan media","https://www.news.com.au/lifestyle/real-life/news-life/sick-new-texts-in-cornell-7-group-leaked-as-global-outrage-mounts/news-story/c2008143ece2464d4158757db4de0955"],", terdapat grup percakapan di Snapchat yang berisi 50 anggota lainnya. Pesan-pesan di dalamnya menceritakan apa yang dilakukan para laki-laki tersebut beserta ajakan kepada yang lain untuk bergabung."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mirisnya, tidak ada satu pun anggota grup tersebut yang melaporkannya ke polisi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketika Jane Doe pertama kali melaporkan kasus ini kepada Kepolisian Universitas Cornell, tidak ada tuntutan pidana yang ",["langsung diajukan","https://abcnews.com/US/district-attorney-reopens-case-alleged-cornell-university-gang/story?id=136806149"],". Namun, Jaksa Distrik Tompkins County membuka kembali penyelidikan setelah gugatan didaftarkan. Ia mengatakan bahwa kasus ini akan dibawa ke dewan juri."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cornell menyatakan ",["penyelidikan internal","https://statements.cornell.edu/2026/20260929-faq.cfm"]," mereka berujung pada sanksi terhadap beberapa mahasiswa yang terlibat, termasuk skorsing dan pengeluaran dari universitas. Selain itu, Chi Phi sampai saat ini masih ditutup. Beberapa laki-laki yang dituduh telah membantah tuduhan tersebut. Sementara itu, anggota lain belum memberikan pernyataan apa pun."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kekerasan seksual sering kali dipandang sebagai tindakan yang dilakukan ",["individu yang “jahat”","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/08862605261432630"],". Namun, penyelidikan yang kini terjadi di Cornell juga menyoroti lingkungan sosial yang menjadi tempat ",["terjadinya kekerasan seksual","https://opal.latrobe.edu.au/articles/report/Primary_Prevention_of_Sexual_Violence_and_Harassment_against_Women_and_Girls_Combining_Evidence_and_Practice_Knowledge_-_Final_Report_and_Theory_of_Change/16590107/1/files/30712574.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pesan-pesan dalam grup tersebut tidak muncul di ruang hampa. Semuanya dikirim dan dibagikan antara teman sebaya, dalam perkumpulan mahasiswa, dalam sebuah universitas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lingkungan institusional seperti ini membentuk apa yang dianggap wajar: apa yang menjadi bahan tertawaan atau kritik, perilaku apa yang mendapatkan persetujuan, keselamatan siapa yang dianggap penting, dan apakah ",["perilaku berbahaya mendapatkan konsekuensi sosial","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33176596/"],". Faktor-faktor inilah yang harus diperhitungkan jika kita ingin mencegah kekerasan seksual."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ini bukan masalah baru"]},{"k":"p","s":["Di Australia, ",["Survei Keamanan Mahasiswa Nasional 2021","https://universitiesaustralia.edu.au/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/2021-NSSS-National-Report.pdf"]," menemukan bahwa satu dari enam mahasiswa pernah mengalami pelecehan seksual. Tidak hanya itu, satu dari 20 mahasiswa pernah mengalami kekerasan seksual sejak mulai berkuliah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Angka tersebut jauh lebih tinggi bagi mahasiswa perempuan, transgender, dan mahasiswa dengan identitas gender yang beragam."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["“Locker room talks”: budaya pelecehan seksual di ruang privat","https://theconversation.com/locker-room-talks-budaya-pelecehan-seksual-di-ruang-privat-281235"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Setelah ",["perjuangan bertahun-tahun","https://doi.org/10.1080/1323238X.2024.2435685"],", Australia kini resmi memiliki ",["Kode Etik Pendidikan Tinggi Nasional untuk Mencegah dan Merespons Kekerasan Berbasis Gender","https://www.education.gov.au/highereducationgbvregulator/nationalcodedevelopment"]," (National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence). Peraturan ini mewajibkan kampus untuk ",["merespons dan menangani","https://www.fairagenda.org/blog_nso_mediarelease"]," penyebab kekerasan seksual sekaligus menciptakan lingkungan yang lebih aman."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kondisi ini menimbulkan pertanyaan penting: bagaimana seharusnya program pencegahan kekerasan seksual dirancang di lingkungan kampus?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terlalu fokus pada individu"]},{"k":"p","s":["Selama ini, pencegahan kekerasan seksual cenderung fokus pada faktor ",["risiko","https://www.taylorfrancis.com/chapters/edit/10.4324/9781003379331-3/thinking-beyond-cultural-change-anna-hush"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pendekatan ini melihat apa saja hal yang dapat membuat seseorang lebih mungkin melakukan atau mengalami kekerasan, serta bagaimana risiko tersebut dapat ",["dikurangi","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/1323238X.2021.1956739"]," Program pencegahan di kampus pun kerap menggunakan pandangan serupa."]},{"k":"p","s":["Berbagai ",["penelitian kami","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/15248380261451846"]," mendapati pendekatan pencegahan kekerasan seksual masih berjalan sendiri-sendiri dan tidak konsisten. Sebagian mahasiswa menerima pelatihan dasar tentang persetujuan, peran saksi yang aktif, dan cara mengenali situasi berbahaya. Sementara itu, mahasiswa lainnya mendapatkan peringatan terkait alkohol dan zat adiktif lainnya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pendekatan yang berfokus pada individu seperti ini dapat mengalihkan tanggung jawab kepada orang-orang yang paling mungkin ",["mengalami","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40462705/"]," kekerasan. Misalnya, perempuan diminta untuk selalu mengawasi ",["minuman","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/14680777.2023.2226831"]," mereka, tetap bersama teman-temannya, mampu mengenali ",["tanda-tanda bahaya","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0955395925000428"]," atau mengatakan “tidak”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Riset: Remaja perempuan yang bepergian sendiri hadapi risiko dan tekanan mental lebih besar","https://theconversation.com/riset-remaja-perempuan-yang-bepergian-sendiri-hadapi-risiko-dan-tekanan-mental-lebih-besar-268564"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Bukan berarti pendekatan-pendekatan tersebut harus dihilangkan. Perannya masih sangat penting. Namun, mengajarkan seseorang untuk mengenali dan menanggapi risiko berbeda dengan mengubah ",["budaya dan sistem","https://learningresources.sagepub.com/blog/epigeum/2025/11/05/going-beyond-compliance---a-student-s-perspective---part-2"]," yang menciptakan risiko tersebut."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mengubah perilaku individu tidak bisa menjadi ",["pendekatan utama","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/15291006231221978"]," dalam pencegahan kekerasan seksual. Oleh karena itu, kita perlu melakukan lebih dari sekadar mengajarkan seseorang caranya menyikapi lingkungan yang tidak aman."]},{"k":"h","s":["Bagaimana kalau kita ubah fokusnya?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Melalui ",["riset terbaru","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/10778012261493148"],", kami berargumen bahwa strategi pencegahan kekerasan seksual harus lebih berfokus pada faktor pelindung berbasis kekuatan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Jika pencegahan berbasis risiko berfokus pada apa yang salah dan cara menghentikannya, pendekatan ",["berbasis kekuatan","https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10896-025-01040-7"]," justru bertanya: apa yang dibutuhkan agar setiap orang merasa aman, terhubung dan sejahtera?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Alih-alih sebatas berupaya mencegah terjadinya kekerasan, pendekatan ini bertujuan untuk ",["membentuk kondisi lingkungan","https://static1.squarespace.com/static/67e9bb2b8ad1d04967a0459c/t/6810270b7b4b430ba2e20147/1745889041212/Protective+Factors.pdf"]," yang sejak awal membuat kekerasan sulit terjadi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Artinya, kita perlu melihat kekerasan seksual lebih dari sekadar perilaku berisiko. Kita harus memperhatikan penyediaan sumber daya, penguatan hubungan, dan penciptaan lingkungan agar mendukung ",["perkembangan","https://www.mdpi.com/1660-4601/20/7/5395"]," masyarakat. Hal ini mencakup jaminan keamanan ekonomi, ",["budaya seksual yang positif","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/00178969261436255"],", komunitas yang mendukung, dan hubungan yang dilandasi rasa kepedulian yang timbal balik."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bidang ",["kesehatan","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/chapter/edited-volume/pii/B9780128142974000121"]," dan ",["pencegahan kekerasan lainnya","https://www.abc.net.au/listen/programs/canberra-mornings/legitimate-sexpectations/101589302"]," sudah lebih dulu menerapkan cara berpikir ini."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tujuannya bukan membuat orang semakin tangguh menghadapi kondisi yang tidak aman. Institusi justru harus bertanggung jawab menciptakan lingkungan yang lebih baik."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bagi universitas, ini berarti tidak hanya melihat apakah mahasiswa sudah menyelesaikan modul tentang persetujuan atau menjadi saksi aktif. Mereka juga harus mencermati apa saja ",["perilaku misoginis","https://doi.org/10.26180/32942816"]," yang diapresiasi atau ditentang di ",["asrama kampus","https://apo.org.au/node/134766"]," dan ",["kelompok-kelompok pertemanan","https://flex.flinders.edu.au/items/dd2ea49a-1977-49e6-ba9f-a4a9f07e5cb6/1/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pihak universitas juga perlu membangun budaya kampus yang mewajibkan adanya kepedulian dan akuntabilitas, sekaligus memastikan bahwa menentang norma-norma yang merugikan tidak berisiko menimbulkan pengucilan sosial."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hal ini juga berarti mendengarkan orang-orang dan komunitas yang paling terdampak oleh ",["kekerasan seksual","https://www.thestopcampaign.org.au/i-deserve-safety"]," untuk memahami apa yang perlu diubah agar mereka merasa aman dan didukung"]},{"k":"h","s":["Pencegahan tidak cukup di permukaan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Laporan pemerkosaan di Cornell memang ",["masih dalam","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-09-29/cornell-university-gang-rape-allegations-new-investigation/107206120"]," proses hukum, tetapi percakapan dalam grup tersebut menimbulkan pertanyaan-pertanyaan yang melampaui kasus ini."]},{"k":"p","s":["Grup percakapan pada dasarnya adalah ruang sosial. Dari sana, terlihat perilaku apa saja yang didukung, ditentang, atau dibiarkan begitu saja tanpa komentar oleh teman-teman sebaya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Semua ini tidak berarti individu lepas dari tanggung jawab atas tindakan mereka sendiri. Tanggung jawab individual dan pencegahan secara struktural bukan dua hal yang bertentangan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, kita tidak bisa menyelesaikan suatu masalah struktural hanya dengan meminta orang untuk mengubah perilakunya. Kita perlu lebih fokus pada apa yang diperlukan untuk mengubah kondisi saat ini menjadi keadaan di mana kekerasan seksual sejak awal tidak terbayangkan bisa terjadi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Jika kamu atau seseorang yang kamu kenali mengalami kekerasan seksual atau kekerasan berbasis gender, bantuan tersedia 24 jam melalui Layanan Sahabat Perempuan dan Anak (SAPA 129) Kementerian Pemberdayaan Perempuan dan Perlindungan Anak di nomor 129 atau WhatsApp 08111-129-129. Pengaduan juga dapat diajukan melalui laman ",["aduan.komnasperempuan.go.id","https://aduan.komnasperempuan.go.id/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ignatia Sarasvati Wahyuputro menerjemahkan artikel ini dari Bahasa Inggris."]}],"chars":7820},"https://theconversation.com/israel-quel-role-pour-les-partis-arabes-apres-leur-percee-historique-aux-legislatives-295813":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"9c82dedfa7c5e614bca923e0556eb65c2d091423c8626f3dcfa7a1b019ec87a9","read":"https://theconversation.com/israel-quel-role-pour-les-partis-arabes-apres-leur-percee-historique-aux-legislatives-295813","bytes":185901,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Israël : quel rôle pour les partis arabes après leur percée historique aux législatives ?","by":[{"n":"Elizabeth Sheppard Sellam","r":"Responsable du programme « Politiques et relations internationales » à la faculté de langues étrangères, Université de Tours"}],"pub":"2026-11-09T16:11:46Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["L’ESSENTIEL"]},{"k":"li","s":["Les partis arabes ont obtenu 19 sièges sur les 120 de la Knesset, contre 10 dans l’assemblée sortante, grâce à une forte hausse de la participation."]},{"k":"li","s":["Mansour Abbas (Ra’am) envisage une participation au gouvernement, tandis qu’Ahmad Tibi (Liste commune) préfère soutenir de l’extérieur une éventuelle coalition dirigée par Gadi Eisenkot."]},{"k":"li","s":["Malgré leur poids parlementaire, les partis arabes se heurtent à leurs divergences idéologiques et aux exigences de leurs partenaires potentiels."]},{"k":"p","s":["Alors que les négociations pour former le prochain gouvernement israélien s’annoncent longues, un aspect du scrutin du 27 octobre retient une attention particulière : la ",["mobilisation des électeurs arabes israéliens et la progression des partis qui les représentent","https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/central-elections-committee-publishes-final-election-results-knesset-to-be-sworn-in-nov-10/"],", à savoir Ra’am et la Liste commune, qui ont remporté à eux deux 19 des 120 sièges de la Knesset (respectivement 8 et 11), contre 10 dans l’assemblée sortante."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ces sièges leur permettront-ils de peser sur les décisions politiques de la prochaine législature ? Mansour Abbas (Ra’am) souhaite intégrer une coalition gouvernementale pour participer à la définition de ses priorités, tandis qu’Ahmad Tibi (Liste commune) envisage de soutenir de l’extérieur un gouvernement dirigé par Gadi Eisenkot, sans y participer. Chacune de ces deux stratégies est confrontée à divers obstacles idéologiques et politiques."]},{"k":"h","s":["Des partis différents, un électorat loin d’être homogène"]},{"k":"p","s":["Les Arabes représentent environ 21 % de la population israélienne, un chiffre qui inclut les druzes dans les statistiques officielles. Majoritairement musulmans, ils comptent également une minorité chrétienne (6,8 %) et des communautés bédouines, principalement musulmanes. Les druzes (environ 7 % de la population arabe dans les statistiques officielles israéliennes), bien qu’arabophones, constituent une ",["communauté religieuse et culturelle distincte","https://www.radiofrance.fr/franceculture/podcasts/questions-d-islam/les-druzes-aux-marges-de-l-islam-1725894"],", dont une partie ne s’identifie pas comme arabe et entretient un rapport particulier avec l’État israélien."]},{"k":"p","s":["Les partis dits « arabes » ne forment pas un bloc homogène, pas plus que la population qu’ils cherchent à représenter. Cette diversité se retrouve dans les choix électoraux : les citoyens arabes ne votent pas tous pour les partis dits « arabes ». Ainsi, en 1992, les formations sionistes recueillaient 52,3 % de leurs suffrages – un ratio qui était encore de ",["14,2 % aux dernières législatives en date, en 2022","https://www.inss.org.il/publication/israel-elections-2022/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Les partis qui ont remporté les 19 sièges présentent eux aussi des orientations différentes. Ils se répartissent entre deux listes réunissant quatre formations. ",["Ra’am","https://en.idi.org.il/israeli-elections-and-parties/parties/raam/"]," est religieux et conservateur. La Liste commune rassemble ",["Hadash","https://en.idi.org.il/israeli-elections-and-parties/parties/hadash/"],", issu du Parti communiste israélien, favorable à la coopération judéo-arabe et soutenu aussi par des juifs ; ",["Ta’al","https://en.idi.org.il/israeli-elections-and-parties/parties/taal/"],", qui défend l’égalité civique et les droits nationaux palestiniens ; et ",["Balad","https://en.idi.org.il/israeli-elections-and-parties/parties/Balad/"],", parti nationaliste palestinien laïque."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sur la définition d’Israël comme « État-nation du peuple juif », les positions sont complexes. Balad est le plus explicite dans son opposition à cette définition et revendique un « État de tous ses citoyens ». Hadash défend également une conception fondée sur l’égalité des droits tandis que Ta’al insiste sur l’égalité civique et les droits nationaux des Palestiniens. Mansour Abbas adopte une approche plus pragmatique : il accepte le caractère juif de l’État comme une réalité politique, sans pour autant y adhérer sur le plan idéologique."]},{"k":"p","s":["Les quatre formations soutiennent la création d’un État palestinien et la fin de l’occupation, même si leurs approches et leurs priorités diffèrent. Hadash défend depuis longtemps la solution à deux États, Ta’al est historiquement proche du mouvement national palestinien et Ahmad Tibi a notamment été conseiller de Yasser Arafat. Balad met davantage l’accent sur les droits nationaux palestiniens et le droit au retour. Ra’am défend également la solution à deux États, mais privilégie aujourd’hui l’amélioration concrète des conditions de vie des citoyens arabes israéliens."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ces différences ont aussi façonné leurs alliances. Réunis en 2015 après le relèvement du seuil électoral, les quatre partis avaient remporté 15 sièges en 2020. Ra’am s’en est séparé en 2021, puis Balad en 2022. En 2026, Hadash, Ta’al et Balad ont reformé la ",["Liste commune","https://en.idi.org.il/israeli-elections-and-parties/parties/the-joint-list/"],", tandis que Ra’am a conservé sa propre liste."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Leur succès en 2026","https://fr.timesofisrael.com/les-partis-arabes-celebrent-des-gains-historiques/"]," tient à la hausse de la participation. Entre 2022 et 2026, elle est passée, dans les localités arabes et druzes, de 53,2 % à environ 77 %."]},{"k":"p","s":["Le rejet de Benyamin Nétanyahou et de ses alliés d’extrême droite Itamar Ben-Gvir et Bezalel Smotrich a contribué à cette mobilisation. Toutefois, réduire ce résultat à un vote contre le gouvernement serait ignorer les préoccupations des électeurs arabes qui portent également, entre autres, sur la ",["criminalité de droit commun dont ils sont souvent victimes","https://fr.timesofisrael.com/manifestation-massive-de-citoyens-arabes-pour-plus-daction-policiere-contre-la-criminalite/"]," et sur ",["leur accès insuffisant aux services publics","https://brookdale.jdc.org.il/en/publication/the-take-up-of-socioeconomic-rights-and-benefits-in-the-arab-population-in-israel/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Deux stratégies pour peser sur le pouvoir"]},{"k":"p","s":["Les divergences entre partis se prolongent dans leur rapport au pouvoir. Nous l’avons dit, deux stratégies se dessinent : participer au gouvernement ou peser sur ses décisions depuis la Knesset."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mansour Abbas défend la première. Dans un ",["entretien publié le 21 octobre","https://qantara.de/en/article/arab-party-leader-2026-israeli-election-we-want-be-party-all-citizens"],", il explique que participer au gouvernement est nécessaire pour répondre aux besoins des citoyens arabes. En 2021, Ra’am était devenu le ",["premier parti arabe indépendant à rejoindre une coalition gouvernementale","https://www.timesofisrael.com/judicial-reforms-recognition-of-bedouin-villages-details-from-coalition-deals/"],", celle de Naftali Bennett et de Yaïr Lapid, qui allait de la droite à la gauche. L’accord prévoyait quelque 53 milliards de shekels (15 milliards d’euros) sur plusieurs années pour les collectivités arabes, en partie dans le prolongement de programmes existants. Tous les fonds n’ont pas été dépensés, mais Ra’am avait pesé sur les priorités gouvernementales. Mais ce précédent date d’avant les massacres du 7 octobre 2023 et les guerres qui ont suivi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Abbas a prolongé cette démarche en 2026 en s’alliant à ",["Yoav Segalovitz","https://www.timesofisrael.com/jewish-former-mk-yoav-segalovitz-announces-unprecedented-run-with-arab-raam-party/"],", ancien député centriste juif et sioniste, ex-responsable de la police, sans adhérer à Ra’am. Leur coopération repose sur la lutte contre la criminalité dans les localités arabes. Avec ses huit sièges, Abbas n’exclut pas une participation au prochain gouvernement, mais reconnaît que les chances d’accord sont faibles."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ahmad Tibi privilégie une autre voie. Le 31 octobre, il a ",["annoncé","https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/veteran-mk-tibi-pledges-arab-parties-support-from-outside-for-a-potential-eisenkot-led-government-i-dont-want-a-ministry-we-want-change/"]," que la Liste commune, forte de 11 sièges, était prête à soutenir sans participation un gouvernement Eisenkot. Elle pourrait appuyer le remplacement du président de la Knesset (actuellement Amir Ohana, du Likoud) et la création d’une commission d’enquête d’État sur le 7-Octobre. Tibi a promis de ne soutenir aucune motion de censure du Likoud ni de provoquer de nouvelles élections. Il invoque le précédent d’Yitzhak Rabin, qui s’était appuyé sur les députés arabes pour faire avancer les accords d’Oslo."]},{"k":"p","s":["Malgré cette différence, le 5e novembre, les deux listes ont ",["recommandé Gadi Eisenkot au président Isaac Herzog pour former le prochain gouvernement","https://www.jpost.com/israel-election-2026/article-913448"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entre divergences idéologiques et refus de coopération"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avec les 19 députés arabes, le bloc d’opposition compterait 67 élus sur 120. Cette majorité parlementaire ne suffit pourtant pas à former un gouvernement. Le premier obstacle est idéologique. La reconnaissance d’Israël comme État juif et démocratique, contestée notamment par Balad, reste fondamentale pour les formations sionistes. Depuis les massacres du 7 octobre 2023, les désaccords sur Gaza, le Hamas et la sécurité compliquent les rapprochements."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avec les 19 députés arabes, Gadi Eisenkot a obtenu les recommandations de 67 élus sur 120 pour former le prochain gouvernement. Mais ce soutien ne garantit pas une majorité gouvernementale. Les deux listes arabes ont choisi de recommander sa candidature malgré des divergences idéologiques persistantes."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Eisenkot maintient quatre conditions","https://www.timesofisrael.com/eisenkot-stands-by-mandatory-service-after-liberman-opens-door-to-ultra-orthodox-parties/"]," pour participer à sa coalition : reconnaître Israël comme un État juif et démocratique, adhérer aux valeurs de la Déclaration d’indépendance, accepter un service militaire ou civil pour tous et reconnaître le Hamas comme une organisation terroriste dont les capacités militaires et gouvernementales à Gaza doivent être démantelées. La conscription divise aussi les ultraorthodoxes et les autres partis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ces exigences ne sont pas les seules difficultés : ",["l’opposition est elle-même divisée","https://www.timesofisrael.com/bennett-golan-pledge-to-back-eisenkot-as-pm-as-bloc-mulls-which-coalition-to-seek/"],". Bennett, allié de Ra’am en 2021, refuse de recommencer, mais soutient Eisenkot. Avigdor Lieberman exclut toute coalition avec Nétanyahou, les partis arabes ou les ultraorthodoxes, tout en refusant de nouvelles élections. Yair Golan défend une coopération avec les partis arabes. Moshe « Bogie » Ya’alon, ancien ministre de la Défense et chef d’état-major, a même ",["proposé de nommer Mansour Abbas ministre","https://x.com/bogie_yaalon/status/2116120963779551491?a=oih0owH6lSCGM5ePHBM&s=19"],", rappelant que ce dernier reconnaît Israël comme État juif et démocratique."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ces divergences politiques ne doivent pas être confondues avec la délégitimation des partis arabes. Après le scrutin, Nétanyahou et le Likoud les ont ",["accusés d’avoir « volé » les élections","https://fr.timesofisrael.com/les-partis-arabes-denoncent-une-campagne-raciste-netanyahu-evoque-des-elections-fausse-par-une-ingerence-etrangere/"],", invoquant des fraudes et une ingérence étrangère. La police ",["n’a pas étayé ces accusations","https://www.jpost.com/israel-election-2026/article-913181"],", et la Commission électorale centrale a défendu la validité du scrutin. Eisenkot a dénoncé ces accusations et le président Isaac Herzog a critiqué la stigmatisation de la communauté arabe. Contester un programme politique est une chose ; contester la légitimité des élus arabes à peser sur les décisions nationales en est une autre."]},{"k":"p","s":["L’absence d’accord de coalition n’exclurait pourtant pas toute coopération : la Liste commune pourrait en tout état de cause ",["soutenir","https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/eisenkot-vows-to-swiftly-exercise-knesset-majority-against-oct-7-government-previews-legislative-agenda/"]," les initiatives d’Eisenkot sur l’enquête d’État du 7-Octobre et la réforme judiciaire."]},{"k":"p","s":["Les électeurs arabes israéliens ont fait entendre leur voix. Reste à savoir dans quelle mesure cette mobilisation leur permettra de peser sur les décisions politiques et de contribuer à tourner la page Nétanyahou, comme ils le souhaitent ouvertement."]}],"chars":9827},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/sri-lanka":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"077e805ae4006763fccd7c3add55f9016ecba729f5ab7359db1c28f8f5e99ac4","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/sri-lanka","bytes":92171,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Sri Lanka travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-15T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-09-21T15:39:53+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Heavy rainfall, flooding and landslides"]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy rainfall during the inter-monsoon season has increased the risk of flooding and landslides across Sri Lanka. Disruption to transport and other services is possible. Check with your travel provider and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sri Lanka Tourism’s 24-hour hotline is available on 1912."]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some flights from Colombo to the UK via Middle Eastern hubs may be delayed, postponed, or re-routed. British nationals in Sri Lanka should check the latest updates from their airlines and consider alternative carriers or routes where necessary."]},{"k":"p","s":["For further information, review ",["Media Notice from the Department of Immigration & Emigration","https://srilankahc.uk/2026/03/02/media-notice-from-the-department-of-immigration-emigration/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Fuel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Government of Sri Lanka is limiting purchases of fuel in response to the situation in the Middle East. All vehicles will be allocated a weekly fuel quota. The Government has announced that special arrangements will be implemented for tour operators and hotels to minimise disruption to tourism."]},{"k":"p","s":["Additional assistance available: Sri Lankan Tourist Hotline: 1912"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/sri-lanka/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Sri Lanka set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Sri Lankan High Commission in the UK","https://srilankahc.uk/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Sri Lanka, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the day you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Sri Lanka, you need to apply for an ‘Electronic Travel Authorization’ (ETA) which is a form of visa."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for an Electronic Travel Authorization (ETA)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Apply for a ",["Sri Lanka ‘Electronic Travel Authorization’ (ETA)","https://www.eta.gov.lk/slvisa/visainfo/extsheta.jsp?locale=en_US"]," online. You should do this before travelling. ETAs are issued free of charge and will be valid for 30 days."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to stay longer, you can apply for an extension online through Sri Lankas ",["official Immigration portal","https://eservices.immigration.gov.lk/vs/home.php"],". You do not need a visa if you are transiting through Sri Lanka by air, if the connecting flight is within 24 hours of your arrival. Check with your airlines about transit times."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information on Sri Lankan visas, please visit ",["Department of Immigration and Emigration","https://www.immigration.gov.lk/index_e.php"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Overstaying your visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you overstay the period of your ETA (30 days), you risk being subject to immigration procedures that may include temporary detention, a fine, deportation at your own expense, a travel ban or refusal of entry to Sri Lanka in the future."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Sri Lanka, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Sri Lanka guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/204/sri-lanka#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Sri Lanka","https://www.customs.gov.lk/personal/travellers/"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Sri Lanka"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most major banks allow Visa and Mastercard cash withdrawals. There are ATMs in major towns and cities, but not all accept international cards."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot transfer money without an exchange control permit issued by the ",["Central Bank of Sri Lanka","https://www.cbsl.gov.lk/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Sri Lanka","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/sri-lanka/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Sri Lanka"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Sri Lanka cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals and tourists such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels"]},{"k":"li","s":["bars, restaurants and night clubs"]},{"k":"li","s":["beaches"]},{"k":"li","s":["tourist sites"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship"]},{"k":"li","s":["large public gatherings, including major events, public holidays, religious occasions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid crowded public places. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["The conflict in Israel and the Palestine has led to heightened tensions around the world. Terrorist groups such as Al-Qaida and Daesh, have called on their supporters to carry out terrorist attacks in response to the conflict. The conflict could also motivate individuals to carry out attacks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks could target Jewish or Muslim communities, or the interests of Israel and its allies. Attacks could also be indiscriminate and occur without warning."]},{"k":"p","s":["On Easter Sunday in April 2019, more than 250 people, including 8 British nationals, were killed in terrorist attacks against 3 churches and 3 hotels in Sri Lanka: in Colombo, Negombo and in Batticaloa."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political and economic situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests and demonstrations can happen anywhere across the island at short notice, and can become violent. Security authorities may use water cannons and tear gas to control protesters."]},{"k":"p","s":["Large-scale protests in 2022 resulted in violence and loss of life. Movement around the island was difficult due to restrictions such as curfews and roadblocks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid demonstrations, political protests or large gatherings. Monitor local media and sign up to ",["get email notifications when this advice is updated","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/sri-lanka/email-signup"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s been an increase in incidents of low-level opportunistic crime. Store your belongings as safely as possible to avoid thefts from hotels and guesthouses. Minimise the number of personal items you carry with you."]},{"k":"p","s":["On the street, criminals may ride past on mopeds or motorbikes and try to snatch your bag. Take care of your passport and money by keeping them in a body-belt. Carry bags on the side of you that is furthest from the road and do not place bags in the front basket of bicycles."]},{"k":"p","s":["Violent crimes against foreigners are rare. Gun crime is not uncommon, but usually it is due to a dispute between different criminal groups."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bank card fraud"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bank card fraud is common."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fraudsters can steal your card details without you noticing. Use ATMs inside banks or hotels if possible, and check ATMs on the street for signs of tampering. Keep cards in sight when paying in shops and restaurants. Read more about ",["how to avoid bank card fraud","https://www.actionfraud.police.uk/a-z-of-fraud/bank-card-and-cheque-fraud"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be alert to the possible use of ‘date rape’ and other drugs including GHB."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not take drinks from strangers or leave your drinks unattended. Victims of spiked drinks have been robbed and sometimes assaulted. Alcohol and drugs can reduce your vigilance, making you less in control. If you drink, know your limit. Drinks served in Sri Lanka are often stronger than in the UK as bars and hotels rarely use measures."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Women continue to report incidents of verbal and physical harassment by men, ranging from sexually suggestive or lewd comments to physical advances and sexual assaults."]},{"k":"p","s":["Incidents can happen anywhere, but the majority of reported cases take place in crowded areas including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["markets"]},{"k":"li","s":["bus and railway stations, or on buses"]},{"k":"li","s":["sporting events"]},{"k":"li","s":["tourist sites"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when travelling alone or in small groups and consider carrying a personal alarm."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must always carry your passport as an official form of identification. A copy is usually acceptable, but in some situations you may have to produce the original at a police station within a specified time limit."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police could fine you if you ignore notices prohibiting alcohol in certain public areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Alcohol is not usually available on religious holidays. Drinking in public on these days could be culturally insensitive. Check locally for dates of religious holidays when this applies."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and e-cigarette bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police could fine you if you ignore ‘no smoking’ signs in certain public areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Sri Lanka use technology to detect illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Detention and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are severe penalties for drug offences, terrorism and all other serious crimes. The authorities could hold you without charge indefinitely. If convicted, you may face a lengthy prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re arrested under Sri Lanka’s Prevention of Terrorism Act, the authorities could detain you without charge awaiting a trial date."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras, binoculars and drones in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not fly drones near, use binoculars to look at, or take photographs of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["military bases"]},{"k":"li","s":["government buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["vehicles used by VIPs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check how to register and operate drones with Sri Lanka’s ",["Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.caa.lk/en/faqs/on-drone-operations#i-am-a-foreigner-who-is-expecting-to-come-to-sri-lanka-to-spend-my-next-vacation-can-i-bring-my-drone-to-sri-lanka-for-my-own-usage"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal, but we are not aware of any prosecutions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress codes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Nude or topless sunbathing is not allowed."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter a Buddhist temple:"]},{"k":"li","s":["cover your legs and shoulders"]},{"k":"li","s":["take off shoes and hats"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Religion"]},{"k":"p","s":["Disrespecting Buddhist images and artefacts, or making offensive remarks about religion, is a serious offence and can lead to arrest. If you have visible tattoos of Buddha, you can be refused entry to Sri Lanka or face deportation. Do not pose for photographs standing in front of a statue of Buddha."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some Sri Lankan animals can be dangerous. If in doubt, follow advice from authorised guides or your travel operator. Wild elephants and crocodiles will attack humans on occasion. Venomous insects and snakes are found in many parts of the country – though not common in populated areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Feral dogs are common and sometimes carry rabies."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many beaches in Sri Lanka have dangerous surf or rip tides at certain times of the year. Get advice from your hotel or tour operator before going in the sea."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Sri Lanka, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],". Tourists can hire cars, tuk tuks and motorbikes to drive. If you hire a vehicle, check that the company you rent the vehicle from is registered with the ",["Sri Lanka Tourist Board","https://srilanka.travel/safe-and-secure"]," and has a ‘Safe & Secure’ certificate. You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have appropriate insurance"]},{"k":"li","s":["ensure that the vehicle is roadworthy before you start your journey"]},{"k":"p","s":["You need a ",["1949 international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and a Sri Lankan ‘recognition permit’ to drive a hire vehicle."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel. Take your UK driving licence and your IDP along with 2 passport photos to:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Automobile Association of Ceylon 40 Sir Mohomad Macan Markar Mawatha Colombo 00300"]},{"k":"p","s":["They will verify your documents and issue a recognition permit. Your hire car company will usually help with this."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some roads, particularly in more remote areas, may be in poor condition. Driving is erratic and there are frequent road accidents, particularly at night. Stay alert for pedestrians and animals on busy roads. Riding a motorbike can be especially dangerous."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have a collision, stay at the site of the accident with your vehicle as long as it is safe to do so. If it is not safe or if you feel threatened, report to a local police station."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are still security checkpoints on main roads in parts of the country. Follow the instructions of the police or army officers on duty. Security forces have opened fire on vehicles that have not stopped when asked. Roads around government and military sites in Colombo are often closed for security reasons, such as access for VIP convoys."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Buses"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public buses are often driven fast, rarely give way and are often poorly maintained leading to serious bus accidents in recent years. Tourist buses are usually driven more professionally and safely, but standards can vary."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can book taxis using local and international taxi apps. There is less availability outside tourist areas. Motorised rickshaws (‘tuk-tuks’) are available for hire in towns and villages. Agree a price before you set off or look for one with a working meter."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are occasional reports of harassment, particularly of women travellers at night. Change to a different tuk-tuk or taxi if you have any concerns about the driver or their standard of driving."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rail travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["When travelling by train, make sure you stay within the train carriage while the train is moving. There have been fatal accidents when visitors have hung out of open doorways or windows of trains. Take care of your personal possessions at all times. There have been incidents of theft and pickpocketing."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["You need prior permission to enter Sri Lankan waters and the security zones in coastal areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["The threat of piracy and armed robbery in the Gulf of Aden and Indian Ocean remains significant. The combined threat assessment of the international Naval Counter Piracy Forces is that all sailing yachts under their own passage should stay out of the ",["designated High Risk Area","https://on-shore.mschoa.org/reference-documents/advice-for-sailing-vessels/"]," or face the risk of being hijacked and held hostage for ransom."]},{"k":"p","s":["See more advice on ",["staying safe when travelling abroad by sea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Monsoon"]},{"k":"p","s":["Monsoon rains can cause flooding in many places in Sri Lanka. Floods can cause widespread displacement of people, injuries and occasional deaths. Heavy rains and landslips can also lead to road closures and affect local transport links."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor Sri Lanka’s Disaster Management Centre and the ",["Sri Lankan Department of Meteorology","https://www.meteo.gov.lk/index.php?lang=en"]," for updates and follow local advice."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tropical cyclones"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of tropical cyclones. Monitor Sri Lanka’s Disaster Management Centre and the World Meteorological Organization for updates."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"h","s":["Northern Sri Lanka"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a visible military presence across the north. Follow local advice and instructions from the security forces and take seriously warning signs about landmines."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Jaffna Peninsula"]},{"k":"p","s":["Operations to clear mines continue, particularly in the heavily mined area towards Elephant Pass. However, apart from High Security Zones, there is free movement."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Kilinochchi, Mullaitivu, Mannar and Vavuniya"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a visible military presence. There was severe war damage to property throughout the northern region, so accommodation options and infrastructure are limited. Follow any local advice about signs warning of mined areas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Eastern Sri Lanka"]},{"k":"p","s":["De-mining and clearance operations are ongoing in parts of east Sri Lanka. There are several areas, primarily former military and police locations, that continue to be marked as minefields. Follow the instructions of the local security forces and look out for signs warning of landmines. Do not leave the roads or cleared footpaths and, if in any doubt, contact the local security authorities for advice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 1990 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Alternatively, contact the Accident Service at Colombo General Hospital on 011 269 1111."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Sri Lanka","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/204/sri-lanka#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Sri Lanka","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/204/sri-lanka"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["chikungunya"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Sri Lanka. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Sri Lanka"]},{"k":"p","s":["Emergency medical treatment outside main cities is not readily available and you may have to be brought to Colombo for treatment. Treatment in private hospitals can be expensive and the options for repatriation to the UK or neighbouring countries in an emergency are limited and very expensive. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Sri Lanka","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/list-of-hospitals"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Sri Lanka"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 011 2691111 or 1990"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire and Rescue: 111"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 118/119"]},{"k":"p","s":["Emergency Police Mobile Squad: 011 5717171"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourist Police: 011 2421052"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Sri%20Lanka"]," or ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Sri%20Lanka"]," in Sri Lanka"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Sri Lanka","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Sri Lanka","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/sri-lanka-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/sri-lanka/british-high-commission-colombo"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/sri-lanka/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Sri Lanka","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-sri-lanka"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":20802,"change":"Addition of information about heavy rainfall, flooding and landslides (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)"},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/lesotho":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"1520a2ee522be35094ade0586c7a33c6799132d1a00723afa0fe103ba1033941","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/lesotho","bytes":47019,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Lesotho travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2012-12-21T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2025-12-10T13:12:05+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/lesotho/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Lesotho’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Lesotho set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Lesotho High Commission Lesotho in the UK","https://www.gov.ls/directory/high-commission-of-the-kingdom-of-lesotho-great-britain/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["All visitors to Lesotho must travel through South Africa, whether travelling by air or land. You need to meet ",["South Africa’s entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-africa/entry-requirements"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Lesotho, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 90 days after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["You need at least 4 blank pages for passport stamping. Lesotho border control need to stamp your passport and so do South African border control on your way to and from Lesotho."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Lesotho for up to 90 days without a visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can extend your stay by completing a ",["90-day temporary permit extension form","https://www.homeaffairslesotho.com/Temporary-Permit-90-Days.html"]," and taking it to the Visa Application Centre in the Manthabiseng Convention Centre, Maseru. Your passport will need to be valid for the extension period."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you overstay without permission, the authorities may detain you and will charge you weekly fines."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Lesotho guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/127/lesotho"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Lesotho. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Lesotho"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques in any currency if the value is 25,000 Lesotho loti or more. If you do not, the authorities could seize your money when you leave and you could be fined."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Lesotho loti is pegged to the South African rand on a one-to-one basis. Both currencies are accepted throughout Lesotho."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK debit and credit cards are widely accepted for payment and at ATMs. If you are travelling outside Maseru, take enough cash to cover local purchases."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Lesotho"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Lesotho, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are occasional political demonstrations in Maseru. These are usually peaceful, but there is a risk of isolated incidents of violence. Move away from demonstrations or gatherings, particularly if you see the security forces are present. Lesotho successfully held elections in 2022 but has had a history which includes political-related violence in past decades."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Much of the violent crime in Lesotho is gun crime between organised crime groups. However, foreigners are vulnerable to opportunistic street crime and vehicle crime."]},{"k":"p","s":["Gender-based violence is very high in Lesotho. Most crimes based on gender are between people who already know each other, but violence towards women and girls happens in all areas of the country."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Mugging and violent vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Muggers can target foreign nationals. Do not walk alone in isolated areas or after dark."]},{"k":"p","s":["Armed carjackers or robbers may try to stop your car or get into it while you are stationary. The danger is greatest in urban areas. Do not stop your car if people try to flag you down and do not give lifts to strangers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep doors locked, windows shut and valuables out of sight. If you are driving across the country:"]},{"k":"li","s":["try to drive during daylight hours"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care near border crossings and at road junctions"]},{"k":"li","s":["be wary of road blocks that need you to stop or slow down"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are caught up in an attack, do not offer any resistance."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Petty theft and burglary"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take precautions to safeguard your valuables and cash. Leave them in hotel safes, if possible. Keep copies of important documents, including your passport’s photo page and entry stamps, in a separate place."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is often an increase in thefts, especially burglaries from villas, leading up to the Christmas and Easter holiday periods."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry a copy of the photo page of your passport and your entry stamp. Officials may ask to see these."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession of drugs is a serious offence and punishments can be severe, including prison sentences."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sexual activity between men is illegal, but FCDO is not aware of this being enforced. Showing affection in public may attract unwanted and negative attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Lesotho for up to 3 months. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards and road conditions in Lesotho are poor. You should drive with caution."]},{"k":"p","s":["Animals roaming on the roads are a hazard, especially at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis and minibuses"]},{"k":"p","s":["Local minibus taxis (‘4+1s’) may be poorly maintained and uninsured. They often ignore road safety rules including speed limits. Avoid using them and steer clear of them when driving."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s safer to use transport arranged by your accommodation or by a tour operator."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical numbers"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need emergency medical assistance during your trip, call 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["If 112 is not operating, call locally on 80093030121."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also access emergency treatment across the border in South Africa. Mediclinic Bloemfontein is a 90-minute drive (140km) from Maseru and has private ambulances."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mediclinic: +27 51 404 6225"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: ER24 +27 102053588"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Lesotho","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/127/lesotho#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Lesotho","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/127/lesotho"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Lesotho. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Lesotho"]},{"k":"p","s":["Lesotho has basic medical facilities. Most foreign visitors use healthcare facilities in Bloemfontein, South Africa, a 90-minute drive from Maseru."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Lesotho, Queen Mamohato Memorial Hospital (+266 2231 3260) and Maseru Private Hospital (+266 2233 3600) are the main hospitals. Both are in the Maseru area. Outside of Maseru there are District hospitals in most of the Districts."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Lesotho","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/lesotho-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Lesotho"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Lesotho"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Lesotho"]," in Lesotho"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Lesotho","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/when-someone-dies-in-lesotho"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Lesotho","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/lesotho-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/lesotho/british-high-commission-in-maseru"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/lesotho/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":10554,"change":"New information about dual nationals returning to the UK (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/paraguay":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"e4c673442f0416e5938712763ec89e189daa53e6da944169a24f708606e7d4e6","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/paraguay","bytes":58255,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Paraguay travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-10T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-03T20:29:30+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/paraguay/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Paraguay’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Paraguay set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Paraguayan Embassy in the UK","https://www.mre.gov.py/embapar-reino-unido/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Paraguay, your passport should be valid for the duration of your stay."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure that an immigration official stamps, dates and signs your passport when you arrive. If you do not have an entry stamp in your passport, you will get a fine when you leave the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is important if you enter Paraguay at a land border, typically the crossing between Ciudad del Este and Foz do Iguaçu in Brazil. Long-distance bus drivers sometimes tell foreign nationals that they can complete immigration formalities in Asunción. This is not true, and you will get a fine if you do not get your passport stamped at the point of entry."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need a visa to visit Paraguay. You will normally get permission to stay for 90 days on arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to stay for another 90 days, check with the ",["Paraguayan Immigration Department","https://migraciones.gov.py/entrada-y-salida-del-pais/"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling to Paraguay to work or study, you should contact the ",["Paraguayan Embassy in the UK","https://www.mre.gov.py/embapar-reino-unido/"]," or check the ",["Ministry of Foreign Affairs visa information","https://www.mre.gov.py/index.php/tramites/visas/consultas-sobre-visas-de-entrada-al-paraguay"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling with children"]},{"k":"p","s":["Children under 18 years of age who are resident in Paraguay need written permission (‘Permiso del Menor’) from the non-accompanying parents to leave the country. The permission is granted by a Justice of the Peace Court, where the applicant resides. You can get more information on requirements for children entering or leaving Paraguay from the ",["Paraguayan Immigration Directorate","https://www.migraciones.gov.py/index.php/tramites/ingreso-y-salida-del-pais/requerimientos-migratorios-de-ingreso-y-salida-del-paraguay-de-menores"]," (in Spanish), the ",["Supreme Court of Justice","https://www.pj.gov.py/contenido/460-autorizacion-para-viajar-al-exterior-de-ninos-ninas-y-adolescentes/460"]," (in Spanish) or from your nearest Paraguayan Consulate."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Paraguay, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Paraguay guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/176/paraguay#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Paraguay","https://www.aduana.gov.py/?page_id=1783"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into and out of Paraguay"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare any cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 US dollars or more. You can ",["make an online declaration in advance","https://www.aduana.gov.py/?page_id=1783"],", or at computer terminals at the airport or place of arrival. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many ATMs accept bank cards. When exchanging money, use registered banks or a bureau de change. Do not change money with people on the street or on arrival at the airport as false banknotes are common."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Paraguay","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/paraguay/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Paraguay"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Paraguay, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Demonstrations and protests"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is often social conflict in Paraguay. There have been calls for demonstrations, which may take place at short notice and cause travel disruption. Demonstrations can occur in any part of the country, including downtown Asuncion, Ciudad del Este and near government buildings, often with little warning. Groups may also set up blockades as a form of protest along the main roads, which can disrupt public transport and lead to widespread delays."]},{"k":"p","s":["If this happens, avoid large gatherings, monitor local media and follow the guidance of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bag-snatching and pickpocketing are a problem on public transport. Many foreigners choose to use taxis rather than take buses. Keep your bags within sight at all times when travelling, and be wary of anyone offering to help you."]},{"k":"p","s":["Muggers are occasionally violent and can be armed. Carrying large amounts of cash or wearing expensive jewellery can make you a target. To reduce the risk of attacks:"]},{"k":"li","s":["use ATMs inside buildings rather than on the street"]},{"k":"li","s":["call a licensed taxi from a landline or a hotel rather than hailing one in the street"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep items like mobile phones and wallets out of sight"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep valuables and passports in a safe place"]},{"k":"p","s":["You might be asked for photo ID if you pay by credit card. Many people choose to carry their photo ID in a money belt under their clothes, to keep it secure."]},{"k":"p","s":["At night, keep away from isolated or poorly lit areas, including in the downtown areas of major cities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Organised crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminal organisations carry out drug trafficking and arms smuggling, often in the border regions. They have also carried out isolated violent attacks in Asunción and elsewhere. These attacks have usually been aimed at the Paraguayan security forces and people associated with rival gangs. Tourists have not been the target of such incidents, but bystanders could be affected."]},{"k":"p","s":["In recent years there has been a small number of high-profile kidnappings. Although foreigners are not routinely targeted, you should be vigilant. See the safety advice for ",["regions of Paraguay","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/paraguay/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Reporting crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["To report a crime, go to the nearest police station, or call the tourist police:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Asunción: (595 21) 446 608 or (595 21) 449 020"]},{"k":"li","s":["Ciudad del Este: (595 61) 502 715"]},{"k":"li","s":["Encarnación: (595 71) 204 102"]},{"k":"li","s":["Salto del Guairá: (595 46) 243 575"]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must always carry ID. Carry a copy or printout of the photo page of your passport, and a copy of your entry stamp."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are resident in Paraguay, the authorities will issue you with an identity card."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are severe penalties for trafficking and possession of illegal drugs. If you are caught in possession of or trafficking drugs, you may get a prison sentence, without bail. Prison standards are poor."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is not illegal and there is a small, active LGBT+ community in Asunción. Same-sex marriages are not recognised in Paraguay. People are likely to disapprove of same-sex couples showing affection in public. Find more information on the websites of LGBT+ organisations like ",["Aireana","https://www.aireana.org.py/"],", ",["Panambi","https://www.facebook.com/panambiparaguay/"]," and ",["SOMOSGAY","https://www.somosgay.org/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Risks at public venues"]},{"k":"p","s":["Safety regulations at public venues may be non-existent or poorly enforced."]},{"k":"p","s":["Food stalls burning fuel and using power cables with poor electricity standards present a constant fire risk in markets. The risk is heightened because markets are often located in narrow streets and can be crowded."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many rivers have strong currents which make them dangerous for swimming. The River Paraguay around Asunción is highly polluted and not suitable for swimming."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check the latest official advice before swimming in Lake Ypacaraí, the tourist destination close to Asunción."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Paraguay, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Paraguay. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have your driving licence and your passport showing the entry stamp with you in the car."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are regular police checks nationwide, usually to check the vehicle and driver’s documents (passport, entry stamp, driving licence) and carry out breathalyser tests. Police checks are common in Asunción, its neighbouring cities and the San Pedro and Concepción departments."]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal blood alcohol limit is 0.00%. If a police officer suspects you of drink-driving, they can confiscate your licence on the spot. If you’re convicted, you can expect a heavy fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are poor and there are often traffic accidents, particularly involving motorbikes. Many motorcyclists drive with no crash helmets."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some vehicles drive with no lights at night. Driving on country roads at night can be particularly dangerous."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drivers in Paraguay often ignore stop signs, traffic lights and speed limits. In many areas, there are no road signs indicating hazards. Road signs are generally poor and can be confusing."]},{"k":"p","s":["Paraguay’s network of paved main roads is limited. Minor and rural roads remain unpaved and are often impassable during the rainy season. Even major paved roads, including in Asunción, can be flooded during heavy rain. Large potholes are a hazard on most roads, including in Asunción."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public transport"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many taxis and buses do not meet European standards and rarely have functioning seat belts."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ‘Terminal de Omnibus Asunción’ is the main bus terminal for long-distance journeys."]},{"k":"hs","s":["River travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many vessels do not meet the health and safety standards that would apply in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy rainfall and flooding can affect several areas, including some areas of Asunción and neighbouring cities. Monitor local media and follow the instructions of local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["During especially hot and dry periods a single spark or flame can start a wildfire. Report fires to the emergency services immediately."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/paraguay"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/paraguay/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Paraguay-Brazil border"]},{"k":"p","s":["Transnational criminal organisations carry out drug trafficking and arms smuggling along Paraguay’s eastern border with Brazil. Most activity is from Pedro Juan Caballero south to Ciudad del Este, and to the Tri-Border Area where the borders of Paraguay, Brazil and Argentina meet."]},{"k":"p","s":["Violent crime is on the increase in this area – take particular care in the departments (‘departamentos’) that border Brazil:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Amambay Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["Concepción Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["Alto Paraná Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["San Pedro Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["Canindeyú Department"]},{"k":"li","s":["Salto del Guairá Department"]},{"k":"p","s":["A small guerrilla-style group calling itself the Ejercito del Pueblo Paraguayo (EPP) operates in the north of the Department of San Pedro and the south of the Department of Concepción. The group typically targets police and the military. They attack the ranches of major landowners, often stealing large numbers of cattle. Their attacks can be violent, and include the use of explosives and firearms. In the last decade, they have kidnapped several high-profile people for ransom, most recently in 2022. Three people are still in captivity."]},{"k":"h","s":["Paraguay-Bolivia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal cross-border activities are common in this area, centred around drug trafficking."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 141 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccinations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip check:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the latest information on ",["vaccination recommendations and health risks in TravelHealthPro’s Paraguay guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/176/paraguay"]]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Paraguay","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/176/paraguay#Other_Risks"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["chikungunya"]},{"k":"li","s":["poor air quality"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need a regular prescription, you should bring enough medication with you."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS has information on ",["whether you can take your medicine abroad","https://www.nhs.uk/common-health-questions/medicines/can-i-take-my-medicine-abroad/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Paraguay"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are some good private medical facilities, but only in the major cities. Hospitals and GPs will expect immediate payment for medical services. Some types of medicines may not be available."]},{"k":"p","s":["Elsewhere, facilities may not meet UK standards. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Paraguay","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/list-of-medical-facilities-in-paraguay"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Paraguay"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 141"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 132"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 911"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Paraguay"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Paraguay"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Paraguay"]," in Paraguay"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Paraguay","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/paraguay-bereavement-death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Paraguay","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/paraguay-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/paraguay/british-embassy-asuncion"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/paraguay/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Paraguay","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-paraguay"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":16185,"change":"Update on possible demonstrations and protests in Paraguay ('Safety and security' page)."},"https://theconversation.com/albanese-and-taylor-focus-their-troops-on-election-as-government-pushes-agenda-through-packed-pre-christmas-sitting-week-296267":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-24T13:28Z","sha":"9370fec4d983828d1faf0277719c916fee625da15533a0bbf6d92d6be91bd230","read":"https://theconversation.com/albanese-and-taylor-focus-their-troops-on-election-as-government-pushes-agenda-through-packed-pre-christmas-sitting-week-296267","bytes":175155,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Albanese and Taylor focus their troops on election as government pushes agenda through packed pre-Christmas sitting week","by":[{"n":"Michelle Grattan","r":"Professorial Fellow, University of Canberra"}],"pub":"2026-11-24T11:02:57Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["It might be only half way through this term, but both the prime minister and opposition leader had the next election firmly in their sights when they addressed their parliamentary troops for the last time this year."]},{"k":"p","s":["With negotiations under way behind the scenes on legislation the government wants the Senate to pass in this final parliamentary sitting week, Anthony Albanese told caucus work had already started for the next election, and he signalled that Labor was thinking about the danger from One Nation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Research had been reported to Labor’s national campaign committee, which had met on Monday, he said."]},{"k":"p","s":["“Significant research has been done on how we deal with the right wing parties that are now competing against each other,” Albanese said."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monday’s meeting is the first held this term by the campaign committee, whose members are drawn from the parliamentary party and Labor’s national executive. Sources said Monday’s discussion focused on how the political environment had changed since the election."]},{"k":"p","s":["While initially One Nation was seen as mainly a threat to the Coalition, Labor now sees itself as having to take on both the Coalition and One Nation."]},{"k":"p","s":["This week’s Newspoll has Labor on a federal primary vote of 27%, One Nation on 27% and the Coalition on 22%."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the joint parties meeting Angus Taylor claimed the government might go to an election next year, rather than in 2028 when it is due."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although that timetable is not being seriously talked about, opposition leaders routinely warn their followers about the possibility of early elections to keep them on their toes and get them into campaign mode."]},{"k":"p","s":["Taylor said, “Make no mistake about it, colleagues – we can win the next election.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["“Because Labor is on the rocks. This government is on the rocks. Australians see this prime minister for who he is – a lying, arrogant, weak, incompetent prime minister.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["He said for the first time voters were “seeing a plan and a team that can fix our economy and protect our way of life.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["The meeting was also addressed by the Liberal federal director Lincoln Folo"]},{"k":"p","s":["Albanese told caucus the government this week wanted to pass the digital duty of care bill, as well as its legislation on trusts and capital gains tax changes for innovative start ups, and its plan for a gas reservation scheme. Soon after the meeting the government announced a deal with the Greens for the passage of the digital duty of care legislation."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government is also hoping for a compromise to pass its cut to the private health insurance rebate for older people. Labor wants seniors to be on the same footing as other people but the Greens have demanded an exemption for pensioners."]},{"k":"p","s":["On Wednesday the government will announce a major treaty with the Solomon Islands. This has involved the Solomon Islands scrapping an earlier 2022 security pact it has had with China."]}],"chars":2836}};
